WEBVTT

00:03.870 --> 00:06.860
The robber was John Doe 
from the Klondike Family.

00:07.380 --> 00:09.570
He's currently being held at the station.

00:11.610 --> 00:14.110
They made yet another mess.

00:14.110 --> 00:15.240
Captain.

00:18.430 --> 00:21.120
By the time I realized it,
 there was this guy in a flashy outfit...

00:21.120 --> 00:22.700
Yeah, yeah! That's him!

00:22.700 --> 00:24.750
I believe he works for Pinochle.

00:24.750 --> 00:28.000
He's always trying to flirt with us.

00:28.000 --> 00:29.480
It's true!

00:32.350 --> 00:33.500
Pinochle...

02:05.850 --> 02:06.640
Captain!

02:06.640 --> 02:10.020
Why aren't we questioning Chris Redgrave?!

02:10.340 --> 02:12.580
He's on the bank's security footage,

02:12.580 --> 02:15.150
not to mention footage of
 the rampage on social media—

02:15.870 --> 02:16.590
Huh?

02:17.790 --> 02:20.870
The criminal was caught 
and the case was resolved.

02:20.870 --> 02:22.650
Let's just leave it at that.

02:23.030 --> 02:28.410
Are we not interrogating him because he's 
an employee of Pinochle Automobiles?

02:28.410 --> 02:31.000
I brought in two men the other day.

02:31.000 --> 02:32.290
Remember them?

02:34.110 --> 02:37.430
Leo Constantine Pinochle and Finn Oldman.

02:38.140 --> 02:40.740
They were also Pinochle employees.

02:40.740 --> 02:42.040
So what?

02:42.040 --> 02:44.930
They have nothing to do with the case, do they?

02:44.930 --> 02:46.430
That's not all!

02:46.750 --> 02:48.680
I looked into it.

02:50.890 --> 02:53.940
There's this. And this. And this too!

02:54.350 --> 02:59.070
Whenever Pinochle employees are involved, 
the cases are mysteriously dropped.

02:59.570 --> 03:01.430
Something must be going on behind the scenes.

03:01.930 --> 03:03.320
"Behind the scenes"?

03:03.320 --> 03:06.340
I'm not sure yet... but I'll find out!

03:06.340 --> 03:09.330
The rookie wants to tell us 
how to do our jobs?

03:09.330 --> 03:12.210
We don't have the time to go
dredging up old cases.

03:12.450 --> 03:16.970
Isn't it our job to right wrongs
 and enforce justice?!

03:16.970 --> 03:20.970
I believe that a thorough investigation 
is in order for Pinochle!

03:23.960 --> 03:27.110
I can't just ignore this
 and pretend I didn't see it.

03:27.770 --> 03:31.300
Once something's on my mind, 
I can't think about anything else.

03:31.980 --> 03:35.480
It bugs me so much, 
I won't be able to sleep at night!

03:37.650 --> 03:39.500
What a temper tantrum.

03:40.740 --> 03:43.030
She hardly sounds like a detective.

03:51.850 --> 03:53.960
Boy, that was rough.

03:53.960 --> 03:55.900
John Doe's interrogation?

03:55.900 --> 03:58.480
All he says is, "Get Captain Young in here."

03:58.480 --> 04:00.070
Could you help me out?

04:00.070 --> 04:01.380
Hmm.

04:02.210 --> 04:03.630
Take her instead.

04:03.630 --> 04:05.390
What? Sugar?

04:05.390 --> 04:07.500
Go act like a detective.

04:10.640 --> 04:12.950
A <i>kid</i>?! Out of the question!

04:12.950 --> 04:14.250
Bring me Young!

04:14.250 --> 04:16.340
Why don't you calm down a bit?

04:16.340 --> 04:18.530
My life is on the line here!

04:18.530 --> 04:21.170
There's no way the family will let me live.

04:21.630 --> 04:23.770
You mean the Klondike Family?

04:24.100 --> 04:26.440
You don't have to worry.
This is a police station.

04:27.800 --> 04:30.620
You obviously don't know anything.

04:31.210 --> 04:34.870
There's no place the family can't reach.

04:35.370 --> 04:36.510
Even in here.

04:37.450 --> 04:40.020
I'm done. I'm finished.

04:40.620 --> 04:42.460
I won't let that happen.

04:43.260 --> 04:46.700
The police aren't what you take them for.

04:49.650 --> 04:51.270
Only a kid would say that.

04:51.270 --> 04:53.850
No, it's not just the kid.

04:53.850 --> 04:56.890
Whoops... No smoking in here.

04:58.930 --> 05:02.030
It's the police's job to right wrongs
 and enforce justice.

05:02.830 --> 05:05.530
You will be judged by the law.

05:05.750 --> 05:06.710
That's right.

05:06.710 --> 05:09.210
We can't have the mafia trampling over us.

05:13.470 --> 05:15.830
Can I really trust you?

05:20.590 --> 05:21.940
F-Fine.

05:21.940 --> 05:23.740
Then let's make a deal.

05:23.740 --> 05:28.750
If you let me escape to safety, 
I'll tell you everything about the family,

05:28.750 --> 05:30.930
from connections to cash flow.

05:30.930 --> 05:31.640
Deal?

05:32.590 --> 05:35.390
And you'll tell the truth about it all?

05:35.690 --> 05:39.770
Sure, as long as you can guarantee my safety.

05:39.770 --> 05:40.820
Very well.

05:41.260 --> 05:43.460
Please apply for witness protection for him.

05:43.460 --> 05:44.410
Got it.

05:45.150 --> 05:48.790
If you could take over from here,
 I have to interview a key witness.

05:52.620 --> 05:56.160
Hey, what exactly is Pinochle?

05:56.930 --> 05:58.920
Why don't you ask that old geezer?

06:09.870 --> 06:11.540
The silent treatment?

06:11.540 --> 06:13.250
It's been a while.

06:13.250 --> 06:14.570
How's everything?

06:16.340 --> 06:20.870
The casino scuffle, 
the bank robbery yesterday...

06:20.870 --> 06:24.210
It all reeks of desperation, 
so I want to know what's up.

06:26.940 --> 06:30.200
I appreciate how serious 
you are about your work.

06:30.200 --> 06:33.970
But put yourself in my shoes for a second.

06:33.970 --> 06:36.040
I barely get to go home these days.

06:37.720 --> 06:42.860
Now, is there a reason for your 
desperation that I'm not aware of?

06:43.640 --> 06:46.590
<i>I don't have a shoulder
for you to cry on, Young.</i>

06:47.660 --> 06:49.680
Excuse me, Theodore.

06:49.980 --> 06:51.480
That guy is a snake.

06:51.480 --> 06:55.180
He'll entangle, constrict, 
and bare his venomous fangs at you.

06:55.180 --> 06:58.510
Even if you're his childhood friend.

07:00.690 --> 07:02.560
Tell me, Theodore.

07:02.560 --> 07:04.570
What's happening right now?

07:05.430 --> 07:07.640
What happened a month ago?

07:09.370 --> 07:11.930
You need to know when to quit, Young.

07:18.990 --> 07:20.830
Welcome, Mr. Apple.

07:20.830 --> 07:22.400
Hello, Finn.

07:22.400 --> 07:24.460
How's your stomach?

07:24.460 --> 07:25.980
My stomach?

07:26.520 --> 07:28.330
Oh, I'm all better now!

07:28.330 --> 07:30.470
Finn, just show him in.

07:33.240 --> 07:36.600
<i>I'm starting an investigation into 
Pinochle's Old Maid Street branch.</i>

07:36.860 --> 07:40.600
<i>Business hours are nine to six.</i>

07:41.070 --> 07:43.260
<i>By seven, the employees all leave work.</i>

07:43.970 --> 07:46.570
<i>There's nothing suspicious
 about their activities,</i>

07:46.980 --> 07:49.530
<i>and I've observed no contact
 with the Klondikes.</i>

07:50.500 --> 07:51.270
<i>However...</i>

07:51.990 --> 07:54.660
I <i>will</i> get to the bottom of this.

08:06.130 --> 08:08.040
Heya, Bobby.

08:08.040 --> 08:09.880
I heard you got real hurt.

08:10.230 --> 08:12.310
I'm worried about you, you know?

08:12.310 --> 08:15.140
Standing out here like an idiot...

08:15.140 --> 08:18.010
Did you get a new job as a doorman?

08:18.010 --> 08:19.790
You bastard.

08:19.790 --> 08:23.820
Don't get cocky just 'cause you've
 known the boss for a long time,

08:23.820 --> 08:25.520
or I'll marble you!

08:27.510 --> 08:30.150
I'm only kidding. It was a joke.

08:30.570 --> 08:32.550
Oh, one more thing.

08:33.570 --> 08:38.120
I hear the one who did you in 
was an amateur and a kid.

08:39.320 --> 08:41.160
Your future's not looking too bright, huh?

08:42.430 --> 08:44.590
Damn it... You bastard!

08:44.590 --> 08:45.510
Leave it!

08:46.650 --> 08:48.350
Don't start something!

08:51.950 --> 08:53.170
Shit...

08:53.170 --> 08:57.860
Shit. Shit! <i>Shit</i>!

09:10.490 --> 09:12.980
<i>Guests from financial tycoons to musicians.</i>

09:13.530 --> 09:17.030
<i>Those are executives from PA Systems.</i>

09:17.390 --> 09:20.350
<i>So they're involved in the 
military industry too...</i>

09:29.010 --> 09:31.030
Ban Klondike.

09:33.620 --> 09:36.700
I don't drink. I prefer this.

09:38.990 --> 09:41.020
Tilt, is <i>it</i> ready?

09:41.020 --> 09:42.390
It won't be long.

09:55.710 --> 09:57.950
A Klondike?! Stop sneaking around!

10:00.220 --> 10:01.450
Play!

10:01.450 --> 10:02.660
I don't like...

10:03.750 --> 10:04.950
working overtime!

10:05.400 --> 10:06.460
Police!

10:06.680 --> 10:07.960
Drop your gun.

10:09.550 --> 10:10.260
Huh?

10:11.980 --> 10:14.340
The progress of mankind has made it

10:14.340 --> 10:18.720
so that reaching the moon
 is no longer a dream.

10:18.720 --> 10:26.660
So how is it that there are still so many
 starving children all over the world?

10:26.660 --> 10:28.520
What's wrong with humanity?

10:28.520 --> 10:30.750
It's utterly deplorable.

10:31.130 --> 10:36.190
These parties have been organized
 to overcome this situation.

10:36.610 --> 10:38.920
This is our thirtieth gathering.

10:39.230 --> 10:43.950
I couldn't have come this far 
without the help of everyone here.

10:43.950 --> 10:46.460
Though there <i>are</i> some 
faces here that I'm sick of...

10:49.570 --> 10:53.340
For example, Attorney General Morris
 right over there.

10:53.560 --> 10:55.740
He and I go way back.

10:55.740 --> 11:00.180
When he was young, he was 
aglow with hopes and dreams.

11:00.530 --> 11:03.680
Now the only thing that's 
glowing is his head.

11:05.060 --> 11:08.600
A charity event hosted by 
a front company for the mafia?

11:08.600 --> 11:10.860
What a joke.

11:11.580 --> 11:14.730
Now then, a toast to our bright future.

11:23.460 --> 11:25.240
Hey, Ms. Detective.

11:25.510 --> 11:28.050
I'm telling you, I can explain.

11:28.050 --> 11:30.170
I'll hear your excuses at the station.

11:34.730 --> 11:38.750
Before we toast, I have 
something entertaining for you.

11:46.370 --> 11:49.850
This man used to be a member of our family.

11:49.850 --> 11:53.920
<i>Used to be</i>... As in, he is no longer.

11:53.920 --> 11:55.320
This is starting to scare me.

11:55.320 --> 11:56.020
Yeah.

11:56.020 --> 11:59.690
But I'm sure he had his reasons.

12:00.530 --> 12:04.210
I want everyone here to hear him out.

12:22.130 --> 12:25.650
So, why did you betray the family?

12:25.650 --> 12:30.270
Th-The family would never
 forgive me for losing a card.

12:30.270 --> 12:32.140
S-So...

12:35.240 --> 12:38.520
Come on. I don't have a gun on me.

12:36.900 --> 12:38.940
<i>I finally got my hands on a lead.</i>

12:38.520 --> 12:40.160
See? You can check for yourself.

12:38.940 --> 12:40.650
<i>I'm not letting it go.</i>

12:40.160 --> 12:41.380
Ms. Detective!

12:40.650 --> 12:44.530
<i>Just what is Pinochle really?
And what's behind it?</i>

12:44.750 --> 12:46.210
I'm going to find—

12:50.740 --> 12:53.330
Earlier, I told you...

12:53.610 --> 13:00.130
that the progress of mankind has made 
the dream of reaching the moon a reality.

13:10.330 --> 13:12.290
I also reminded you

13:12.600 --> 13:16.260
that there are still many 
people out there struggling.

13:23.030 --> 13:24.610
Hey! Hey!

13:24.610 --> 13:25.860
Are you okay?! Hey!

13:26.130 --> 13:28.530
Y-Yes, I'm fine...

13:33.370 --> 13:35.080
We gotta get out of here.

13:35.900 --> 13:38.250
Ms. Detective, uncuff me!

13:39.050 --> 13:39.980
Make it quick!

13:39.980 --> 13:41.250
I got it!

13:41.250 --> 13:42.780
Are you done? Hurry up!

13:42.780 --> 13:44.380
Don't rush me!

13:45.970 --> 13:46.760
You're free!

13:50.250 --> 13:56.770
Hand in hand, we must trust 
each other and come together.

13:57.550 --> 14:00.510
We used to be one family.

14:01.020 --> 14:05.210
And I absolutely refuse 
to tolerate division among us!

14:16.710 --> 14:17.780
Play!

14:23.420 --> 14:25.010
Wh-What in the world?!

14:26.170 --> 14:27.550
Who are you?!

14:28.100 --> 14:31.850
Oh, so you're a puppy from Pinochle.

14:32.940 --> 14:36.060
We can start right here, right now!

14:36.060 --> 14:38.110
Our true union!

14:38.830 --> 14:43.370
Let us take that first 
step together, everyone!

14:47.440 --> 14:48.710
Stop!

14:48.710 --> 14:50.470
Come any closer and I'll shoot!

15:01.690 --> 15:02.630
D-Damn...

15:02.630 --> 15:04.250
What's going on?!

15:21.150 --> 15:23.190
No... No way...

15:23.190 --> 15:25.660
Stop this right now! Stop it!

15:25.660 --> 15:26.980
Why can't I move?!

15:26.980 --> 15:28.240
Damn it!

15:28.240 --> 15:29.100
Come on...

15:29.100 --> 15:31.910
Stop! Don't do this!

15:33.960 --> 15:36.160
My speech ran a bit long.

15:43.420 --> 15:45.530
Thank you for listening.

15:47.010 --> 15:49.670
Once again, cheers.

15:53.510 --> 15:56.810
I'm sorry, but I don't drink.

16:04.780 --> 16:06.610
This is a warning.

16:06.610 --> 16:09.620
Don't meddle in the
 family's affairs.

16:09.620 --> 16:14.970
If you point a gun at me again,
 I'll take your life.

16:26.210 --> 16:29.250
Oh. I didn't know you were here, Young.

16:30.780 --> 16:32.910
Are you interested in charities?

16:32.910 --> 16:35.220
No, I'm here on other business.

16:35.220 --> 16:35.970
Oh?

16:37.190 --> 16:39.780
The attack on Trapla Palace.

16:40.760 --> 16:45.740
It was a month ago, when King Julius Fourland
announced his abdication.

16:46.090 --> 16:48.990
The cards were secretly 
assembled at the palace

16:48.990 --> 16:51.480
for the coronation of the next king.

16:52.030 --> 16:56.190
You Klondikes found out and 
attacked the palace that day.

16:56.190 --> 16:57.250
Isn't that right?

16:58.990 --> 17:01.430
Where are the cards now?

17:01.890 --> 17:02.920
Who knows?

17:06.220 --> 17:10.980
Since the attack on the palace, 
more players are appearing on the streets.

17:11.390 --> 17:16.510
I don't think you'd be handing cards out,
 and Theodore won't tell me a thing.

17:16.510 --> 17:18.290
Quite frankly, I'm at a loss.

17:19.260 --> 17:20.140
Hey...

17:20.950 --> 17:23.890
What's going on in Fourland right now?

17:24.820 --> 17:26.520
That night a month ago...

17:27.380 --> 17:29.100
What really happened?

17:30.750 --> 17:33.030
This isn't like you, Young.

17:33.030 --> 17:36.580
I wanna know. I can't help myself.

17:36.580 --> 17:39.030
Must be the nature of a detective.

17:41.770 --> 17:44.410
Please, I need to know.

17:46.940 --> 17:48.740
X-Blind.

17:48.740 --> 17:50.410
"X-Blind"?

17:50.410 --> 17:54.420
History repeats itself.

17:55.580 --> 17:59.080
Don't you want to see Fourland burn in hell?

18:02.040 --> 18:04.820
Do not trust Theodore.

18:04.820 --> 18:08.360
He'll bite your throat someday if you do.

18:09.740 --> 18:15.510
Can't we drink together like we used to?

18:16.290 --> 18:17.790
Did you forget?

18:17.790 --> 18:19.580
I don't drink.

18:30.050 --> 18:31.710
What in the world is going on?!

18:31.980 --> 18:33.590
I don't understand!

18:33.590 --> 18:35.340
You and that woman...

18:35.340 --> 18:36.840
What's happening?!

18:37.110 --> 18:39.190
Hey, calm down.

18:43.020 --> 18:46.430
It's the police's job to right wrongs
 and enforce justice.

18:47.250 --> 18:49.640
But I'm scared!

18:52.330 --> 18:55.150
You should keep your distance from us.

18:56.270 --> 18:57.730
For your own good.

18:59.180 --> 18:59.860
No.

18:59.860 --> 19:01.010
Huh?

19:01.010 --> 19:02.620
Because I...

19:02.890 --> 19:04.370
It'll bug me.

19:04.750 --> 19:07.410
I can't help but be curious.

19:08.570 --> 19:11.880
I can't pretend like it didn't happen.

19:12.250 --> 19:15.380
<i>I can't just ignore this
 and pretend I didn't see it.</i>

19:15.380 --> 19:17.130
<i>I won't be able to sleep at night!</i>

19:19.410 --> 19:22.070
That's why I will—

19:24.760 --> 19:25.480
Huh?

19:26.390 --> 19:28.710
You need to cool your head.

19:29.370 --> 19:30.320
See ya.

19:30.320 --> 19:31.640
W-Wait!

19:43.310 --> 19:45.270
The rain stopped.

19:54.290 --> 19:56.450
Finn Oldman, huh?

19:57.050 --> 19:58.800
Is something wrong?

20:00.740 --> 20:03.050
No. Let's get back to the station.

20:03.270 --> 20:04.070
Sir.

20:09.150 --> 20:11.460
Am I stupid?

20:12.180 --> 20:14.020
I can't stop thinking about it.

20:14.360 --> 20:17.960
Ever since I was small, once I get 
something in my head, I can't help it.

20:18.780 --> 20:21.110
People always made fun of me.

20:21.430 --> 20:23.620
I'm sure I must've been annoying.

20:23.980 --> 20:26.890
But I didn't know how to stop.

20:27.660 --> 20:32.790
One time, I found a typo in an article, 
so I wrote to the newspaper.

20:32.790 --> 20:35.960
They sent me pencils as a thank-you.

20:35.960 --> 20:37.660
I was so happy.

20:38.010 --> 20:41.170
It felt like I was being acknowledged 
for the first time.

20:42.900 --> 20:46.450
That feeling is why I aspired 
to become a police officer.

20:47.980 --> 20:49.730
Does that make me a bad detective?

20:50.750 --> 20:53.780
I didn't have a good reason either.

20:54.590 --> 20:58.300
The world exists in a fine balance.

20:59.610 --> 21:04.360
The smallest tip of the scales 
leads to chaos and despair.

21:05.420 --> 21:09.820
Our job is to keep our eyes on those scales.

21:10.600 --> 21:12.360
I'm not sure what you mean.

21:21.070 --> 21:24.010
John Doe, the guy I left you in charge of...

21:24.130 --> 21:27.030
He was found dead this morning.

21:27.970 --> 21:28.940
What?

21:31.070 --> 21:34.870
Still, I have high hopes for you.

21:52.300 --> 21:54.370
We lost John Doe.

21:54.370 --> 21:58.190
But it was a necessary sacrifice 
for us to move forward.

21:59.130 --> 22:01.540
Are you ready?

22:01.880 --> 22:04.200
All is for the family.

23:36.500 --> 23:39.180
Next time: "TAKE BACK FIVE."
